evitaDB - Vendored third-party source in evita_engine
=====================================================

Snowball Polish stemmer
-----------------------

`io.evitadb.index.fulltext.analysis.PolishSnowballStemmer` is a modified copy of
`org.tartarus.snowball.ext.PolishStemmer` from the Apache Lucene project
(https://lucene.apache.org), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
That file is itself generated by the Snowball compiler from `polish.sbl` of the
Snowball project (https://snowballstem.org), licensed under the BSD 3-Clause
License.

Copied from the Lucene main checkout at commit b26f7672981 (2025-12-18), which
vendored the Snowball 3.0.0 output of `polish.sbl`. The Lucene release this
project pins (9.12.3) predates that commit, which is why the class is vendored
rather than depended upon.

Modifications by FG Forrest, a.s. for evitaDB:
  - Package and class renamed to io.evitadb.index.fulltext.analysis
    .PolishSnowballStemmer, so that the copy does not shadow the upstream class
    once a pinned Lucene release carries it.
  - Private go_out_grouping / go_in_grouping shims copied from Lucene main's
    org.tartarus.snowball.SnowballProgram, because the 9.12.3 runtime predates
    Snowball 3.0's generated-code contract and lacks those two methods.

No other change was made to the generated algorithm.

